# Osprey

The osprey is a large fish-eating raptor found on every continent except
Antarctica. It hunts on the wing, quartering over open water and hovering before
a feet-first plunge that carries it briefly under, and it will catch fish
weighing a third of its own body mass. The talons close on the fish with two
toes forward and two back, and the catch is carried head-first to reduce drag.
A large stick eyrie is used for many years and added to each season. See
[[pandionidae]] and [[accipitriformes]].
